target: internal/report/report.go
verify: go test ./internal/report/ -count=1 -run 'TestParityWithPrReport/a_roster_findings_count_that_is_an_empty_list$'
expect: --- FAIL:
why:    an empty container is FALSY in Python, so `[] or ""` and `{} or ""` are both "", and the report renders nothing. This is a PRESENCE divergence rather than the punctuation one the enumerated list already covers for non-empty containers: measured against the oracle, `"findings": []` renders "ok,  finding(s)" there and "ok, [] finding(s)" here, and `"status": {}` the same. This entry removes the test ENTIRELY, so it guards the divergence existing at all; report-empty-container-matched-by-spelling guards the weaker form, where the test is present but matches a spelling and so misses `[ ]`. Two entries because they are two defects: one renders the text for every empty container, the other only for the ones a writer spelled with whitespace. `isEmptyContainer` goes unreferenced here, which compiles — Go rejects an unused local, not an unused function.
--- old
	if isEmptyContainer(b, t) {
		return ""
	}
--- new
